From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: iasnezhkov <iasnezhkov@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 04:12:58 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 24/27] v4l2: call libdpframework's real DpBlitStream
 destructor

Every MDP decode session left two dma-buf fds open in
android.hardware.media.c2-service-v4l2: one system-heap buffer (3060 kB,
the tiled source) and one mtk_mm "Gralloc" buffer (3064 kB, the
destination), 2/4/6/8 after four AVC/HEVC surface sessions on 28.09
(dmabuf_dump, /proc/<pid>/fdinfo exp_name). strace -f -y of one session:
the decoder thread dup()s the source and destination fds right before
the first MDP ioctl (the recording frame), and nothing closes the dups.
v4l2_codec2 itself never calls dup; libdpframework does when a buffer is
registered with DpBlitStream::setSrcBuffer/setDstBuffer, and releases
them in ~DpBlitStream.

That destructor never ran. The local declaration of DpBlitStream (the
blob has no header here) declared only the constructor, so the explicit
stream->~DpBlitStream() in ~MdpImageConverter bound to the implicit,
trivial destructor of the local declaration and compiled to nothing.
Declaring the destructor makes the call resolve to the blob's exported
_ZN12DpBlitStreamD1Ev (nm -D: C1/C2 at 0x82bc8, D1/D2 at 0x82dc4, no
deleting D0, so it is not virtual and the direct call is the right one).

Test: CodecRig decode AVC and HEVC surface x4, dmabuf_dump of the service
after each: 0 held (before: +2 per session); translate_fd 0; 150/150.
---
 v4l2/MdpImageConverter.cpp | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/v4l2/MdpImageConverter.cpp b/v4l2/MdpImageConverter.cpp
index 8a3c108..6adcdb7 100644
--- a/v4l2/MdpImageConverter.cpp
+++ b/v4l2/MdpImageConverter.cpp
@@ -27,6 +27,7 @@ struct DpRect;
 class DpBlitStream {
 public:
     DpBlitStream();
+    ~DpBlitStream();
     int setSrcConfig(int width, int height, DP_COLOR_ENUM color, DpInterlaceFormat interlace,
                       DpRect* roi);
     int setSrcBuffer(int fd, unsigned int* planeSizes, unsigned int planeCount);
